    state verified
    statement """
        Copy path in the shell rendered the path through Files.Actions1 and reported "Copied path: …" without any clipboard write, and nothing caught it: the transport is a spawned wl-copy, so no unit test can observe the clipboard, and the notice text was the only "evidence" the feature worked. A notice should be derived from the transport's result, and any surface that claims to have put something on the clipboard needs a route that fails loudly when it did not.
        """
