record legeos.papercut.in-a-shared-working-tree-cargo-test-p-lege-and/1 : papercut {
    title "In a shared working tree, `cargo test -p lege` and `cargo check -p…"
    state verified
    statement """
        In a shared working tree, `cargo test -p lege` and `cargo check -p lege` are only as green as every other lane's in-flight edit: mine failed twice on other lanes' half-edits in cli/lege/src/dev (a missing report::identities_as_json, then a BuildSet/SetManifest `provenance` field the gates.rs fixtures had not caught up with) despite nothing of mine being involved. Retrying a minute later worked both times, but a lane cannot tell "my change broke it" from "someone else is mid-edit" without reading the error.
