record legeos.papercut.templaros-install-free-space-dev-nvme0n1/1 : papercut {
    title "templaros-install --free-space /dev/nvme0n1 refused: 'is a partition'.…"
    state verified
    statement """
        templaros-install --free-space /dev/nvme0n1 refused: 'is a partition'. lsblk -no PKNAME on a disk lists child partitions' PKNAME, so the check is always true for a partitioned NVMe. Fix: lsblk -dno PKNAME. Live workaround: sudo sed -i 's/lsblk -no PKNAME/lsblk -dno PKNAME/g' /usr/libexec/templaros/provision
        """
    observed_at git:e7458c3a132ed5ad8cd93f40d808bf2cef9456d4
    author "grok"
    created_at 2026-09-11
}

record legeos.papercut.tests-integration-nested-session-sh-deleted-its/1 : papercut {
    title "tests/integration/nested-session.sh deleted its own temp root on every…"
    state verified
    statement """
        tests/integration/nested-session.sh deleted its own temp root on every exit, including failures, so "socket did not appear" arrived with no compositor log to read and cost a reproduce-by-hand round trip. Worse, the `exit $?` meant to carry the status could never run: the script is `set -e`, so a failing `dbus-run-session` left the shell before that line. Fixed both (keep on failure, `|| status=$?`) — but the pattern is worth checking for elsewhere: a bare command whose exit status is read on the following line is a no-op under `set -e`.
        """
    observed_at git:d9ab0344cdb3af1778b584c03b0ccf8707452bb8
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-04
}

record legeos.papercut.the-acceptance-command-just-image-summary/1 : papercut {
    title "The acceptance command `just image summary` cannot be run without side…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The acceptance command `just image summary` cannot be run without side effects on someone else's file: the recipe's first line is `./distro/image/compose.sh`, which rewrites the generated `mkosi.conf.d/50-seeds.conf` from `distro/seeds/*.seed`. Validating a change to `mkosi.repart/*.conf` therefore also regenerates the package list, which is a different concern and a different owner. A `just image mkosi-only` (or a `--no-compose` flag) would let a repart change be checked on its own.
        """
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-03
}

