    state verified
    statement """
        The working tree carried a body of in-flight work that did not compile (a borrow error in the portal's new dialog.rs) and had three failing shell tests, so `git status` looked like ordinary uncommitted progress while `cargo check` was broken. Running the gates before trusting a dirty tree cost a while; a pre-commit hook, or a note in the handoff that the tree is mid-change and red, would have said so up front.
        """
    observed_at git:06bf665f54b58b218e145fb66f8d4033e53e39bc
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-30
}

record legeos.papercut.the-workspace-stopped-building-entirely-because/1 : papercut {
    title "The workspace stopped building entirely because the sibling repo…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The workspace stopped building entirely because the sibling repo deleted the crate we point at: bpg-rs commit c8ebe3f removed crates/bpg-decode ('still265 carries the only copy'), so every cargo command failed on 'failed to load manifest for dependency bpg-decode'. Repointed the workspace dep to { package = \"still265\", path = \"../bpg-rs/crates/still265\" } and aliased the HEIC helpers through its internal compat module. This is the unpinned-sibling risk CLAUDE.md already names, now realised: the deps should be pinned git revs before packaging.
        """
    observed_at git:a9cc77b6d8c8149fca1527dd772e4457bac8079d
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-08
}

record legeos.papercut.third-bug-in-the-same-chain-after-the-machine/1 : papercut {
    title "Third bug in the same chain: after the --machine fix, lege-resourced…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Third bug in the same chain: after the --machine fix, lege-resourced restarted fine but the activation gate still reported "came back without writing a build stamp". Root cause: RealStamps::read() (cli/lege/src/dev/systemd.rs) called lege_build::read_stamps(), which resolves its directory from the CURRENT process's own $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR -- root's (unset under sudo), not the desktop user's /run/user/<uid>/legeos/build where user-scope units (everything except hostd/boot-health) actually write. Confirmed by hand: /run/legeos/build does not exist at all; /run/user/1000/legeos/build/lege-resourced.json does, freshly written. Fixed by having RealStamps merge /run/legeos/build (system scope) with the target user's resolved /run/user/<uid>/legeos/build (user scope, uid read from /etc/passwd via SUDO_USER) when running as root.
        """
    observed_at git:f5007ef369d0b386fb872a6b726e3f8baaac5944
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-01
}

record legeos.papercut.tracing-subscriber-fmt-writes-ansi-colour-codes/1 : papercut {
    title "tracing_subscriber::fmt writes ANSI colour codes into journal MESSAGE…"
    state verified
    statement """
        tracing_subscriber::fmt writes ANSI colour codes into journal MESSAGE fields of every templar unit (journalctl -o json returns them as byte arrays and they split 'templar_resourced::daemon: tick'), so anything parsing the journal must strip CSI sequences; disabling ANSI when JOURNAL_STREAM is set would avoid it.
        """
    observed_at git:50af3784cb5c3f0ebe72a1e15f12a88f57e11290
    author "sonnet-triage"
    created_at 2026-10-01
}

record legeos.papercut.triaging-the-2026-10-01-freeze-as-the-desktop/1 : papercut {
    title "Triaging the 2026-10-01 freeze as the desktop user: `journalctl -k`…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Triaging the 2026-10-01 freeze as the desktop user: `journalctl -k` printed nothing and no error, because provision.sh created the account in sudo,video,render only (not adm/systemd-journal), so every kernel and system-unit line of the frozen boot needed sudo. provision.sh now adds adm; machines installed earlier need scripts/freeze-evidence-setup.sh.
        """
    observed_at git:50af3784cb5c3f0ebe72a1e15f12a88f57e11290
    author "sonnet-triage"
    created_at 2026-10-01
}

record legeos.papercut.unprivileged-libarchive-dev-extraction-has/1 : papercut {
    title "Unprivileged libarchive-dev extraction has libarchive.so ->…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Unprivileged libarchive-dev extraction has libarchive.so -> libarchive.so.13.8.5; that exact versioned runtime soname must resolve to the installed runtime. A dangling symlink made rust-lld select libarchive.a even with dylib=archive, producing many unrelated-looking codec symbol errors.
        """
    observed_at git:2bc8f741f3c21759c3e7c728d9c211868035aa18
    author "omp"
    created_at 2026-10-03
}

record legeos.papercut.ux-papercut-in-the-same-session-lege-dev-deploy/1 : papercut {
    title "UX papercut in the same session: `lege dev deploy`'s success and…"
    state verified
    statement """
        UX papercut in the same session: `lege dev deploy`'s success and failure output were visually indistinguishable -- a failure bail!()s the ENTIRE accumulated progress log as one anyhow error, so it prints almost identically to a successful run except for a "lege: " prefix on line 1 alone and two trailing lines. Fixed cli/lege/src/dev/mod.rs deploy() to prepend "DEPLOY FAILED -- package state changed, activation did not" to the bailed message, and append "deploy succeeded" to the genuinely-successful output.
        """
    observed_at git:f5007ef369d0b386fb872a6b726e3f8baaac5944
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-01
}

record legeos.papercut.wayland-scanner-0-31-panics-on-any-xml-entity/1 : papercut {
    title "wayland-scanner 0.31 panics on any XML entity reference in a protocol…"
    state verified
    statement """
        wayland-scanner 0.31 panics on any XML entity reference in a protocol file ("Ill-formed protocol file: Ok(GeneralRef(...))") with no line number and no mention of the entity; a `&lt;` in an arg summary took the whole shell's generated bindings down at 56b890a until d3c0cd9 rewrote it. A gate that greps interfaces/wayland/*.xml for `&[a-z]+;` would turn the panic into one sentence.
        """
    observed_at git:37033447950b39b2f9238f5c8ff0bff56ebb23fd
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-10
}

